      "answer": "At Aureum, the conflicting SCIM fields were `department` and `businessUnit` [art_79f625aafa16]. Jin said some payloads included `department` while others included `businessUnit`, and Tess gave the concrete examples `businessUnit=merchant` for Merchant Services and `department=payments` for Payments Ops [art_79f625aafa16].\n\nJin\u2019s fast fix was to add a preprocessing rule in Signal Ingest that maps `businessUnit -> department` or the reverse, then publish a normalized field for the correlator [art_79f625aafa16]. He described that as a config-only, hot-reloadable change, so Aureum could avoid waiting on the longer Okta source-standardization path, which would require change control and might take 2\u20134 weeks [art_79f625aafa16].",
