      "answer": "This is not a MapleBridge one-off; there\u2019s a recurring Canada approval-workflow pattern across multiple customers. [art_f4a8c516b934][art_cbfb5f92862c][art_6be1b68b59cb][art_39c1434aa40a][art_e9c20e0a23e0][art_981952a71434][art_b86a0ca2ce1e]\n\nThe customers showing that pattern are:\n- MapleBridge Insurance [art_f4a8c516b934]\n- City of Verdant Bay [art_cbfb5f92862c]\n- Maple Regional Transit Authority [art_6be1b68b59cb]\n- MapleBay Marketplace [art_39c1434aa40a]\n- MapleFork Franchise Systems [art_e9c20e0a23e0]\n- MaplePath Career Institute [art_981952a71434]\n- MapleWest Bank [art_b86a0ca2ce1e]\n\nIn plain English, the shared failure pattern is that Canada-specific approval rules were supposed to take priority, but the system instead used the global or default rule, so Canada or province-specific approvers got skipped, approvals got stuck or denied, or requests were routed to the wrong approvers. That usually shows up after a migration or a rule-evaluation/normalization change. [art_f4a8c516b934][art_cbfb5f92862c][art_6be1b68b59cb][art_39c1434aa40a][art_e9c20e0a23e0][art_981952a71434][art_b86a0ca2ce1e]\n\nMapleBridge\u2019s specific version of that same pattern was Canada approvers being bypassed after the 2026-03-12 migration because `canada.v2` overrides conflicted with `global.v3` default rules, with delayed SI-SCHEMA-REG sync across the evaluation cluster contributing to it. [art_f4a8c516b934][art_54e35e2cb431][art_e697b3abe158]",
